We might just be able to pull this off!

258
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:51,990
Remarkable!

259
00:17:52,073 --> 00:17:53,457
Take a look at his skin.

260
00:17:53,540 --> 00:17:55,893
It's completely regaining all its color.

261
00:17:57,680 --> 00:17:59,340
His skin is filling out.

262
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,660
My god, brain activity too.

263
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:05,220
I don't believe it.

264
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:07,145
His vitals are stable as well.

265
00:18:10,920 --> 00:18:11,840
His eyes!

266
00:18:12,020 --> 00:18:13,138
He opened his eyes!

267
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:15,040
We did it! He's back!

268
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:22,460
Old man.

269
00:18:32,980 --> 00:18:35,220
You're a damn fool, Jotaro!

270
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,820
You have got to be kidding!

271
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:39,970
Hmm.

272
00:18:40,053 --> 00:18:42,192
All you've done is resurrect yours truly!

273
00:18:42,860 --> 00:18:46,317
Bastard! Wait! Calm down,
Jojaro! It was a joke!

274
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:47,518
I was just kidding!

275
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,484
There's no need to get violent!

276
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:51,400
I'm sorry!

277
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,557
I was just trying to have some fun!

278
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,640
You have my word! It's me!

279
00:18:56,040 --> 00:18:57,340
I'm Joseph Joestar!

280
00:18:57,620 --> 00:19:00,160
I was born September 27th in 1920!

281
00:19:00,700 --> 00:19:04,120
My wife's name is Suzy Q, and
I collect comics as a hobby!

282
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:07,040
I have a question for you.

283
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:10,404
Who's the leading actress
in Tarzan the Ape Man?

284
00:19:10,540 --> 00:19:11,440
Bo Derek!

285
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:13,517
Okay, now answer this one.

286
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,717
Who sang Eat It, the spoof of Beat It?

287
00:19:15,800 --> 00:19:17,360
Weird Al Yankovic!

288
00:19:17,560 --> 00:19:18,600
Good grief.

289
00:19:18,840 --> 00:19:19,920
It has to be you.

290
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:22,747
Who else would know
pointless crap like that?

291
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,080
This is Card, over!

292
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,220
It's amazing! Mr.

293
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:28,772
Joestar is back with us!

294
00:19:29,080 --> 00:19:31,197
He's come back from the brink of death!

295
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:33,240
It's a miracle! Over!

296
00:19:34,940 --> 00:19:36,000
Hear that?

297
00:19:36,360 --> 00:19:39,066
We've taken back everything
you stole from us.

298
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:40,280
Do you?

299
00:20:09,520 --> 00:20:11,320
It's finally over.

300
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,860
Dio took something
precious from all of us.

301
00:20:20,160 --> 00:20:23,160
For a hundred years, he's
taken whatever he wanted.

302
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,620
His appetite for power
has been insatiable.

303
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,320
He's taken far too much.

304
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:30,700
You realize that?

305
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:36,379
Yeah, he's taken things from us that
we'll never be able to get back.

306
00:20:37,380 --> 00:20:42,204
The losses that we've endured on this
journey stretch as far as the planet itself.

307
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,417
But thanks to their sacrifices,

308
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:48,940
we're here to tell the tale
and carry on in their stead.

309
00:20:54,240 --> 00:20:56,040
Kakyoin. Iggy. Avdol.

310
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:58,460
It's over.

311
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:12,282
So you're really going
back to France, Polnareff?

312
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,580
This may be a bit forward,
but your family's gone.

313
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:19,548
Why don't you come back
with me to New York?

314
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,330
Mr.

315
00:21:22,413 --> 00:21:26,453
Joestar, I know they're gone, but
France is the only home I've ever known.

316
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:28,389
It's filled with memories.

317
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:31,700
It's a place I must return
to no matter where I go.

318
00:21:32,460 --> 00:21:34,225
But if you ever need anything,

319
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:37,929
all you have to do is call and
I'll be there in a heartbeat.

320
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:40,107
We're gonna miss you, buddy.

321
00:21:45,060 --> 00:21:47,360
It wasn't easy, that's for damn sure.

322
00:21:48,260 --> 00:21:50,037
But I had a hell of a time,

323
00:21:50,120 --> 00:21:53,591
and I'm lucky to have been on
this adventure with you guys.

324
00:21:55,460 --> 00:21:59,260
Remember, we're a team, and
that's never gonna change.

325
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:04,133
Calling all passengers for
France International Airlines.

326
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:05,520
Flight 92 to Paris.

327
00:22:06,020 --> 00:22:07,640
Please proceed to gate 18.

328
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:10,060
Avianto, you ornery bastard.

329
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:11,536
Live long and happy.

330
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:15,060
And you as moody grandson,
you'd better not forget me.

331
00:22:15,300 --> 00:22:16,320
We'll meet again.

332
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:19,437
That is, of course, if you
don't hate my guts by then.

333
00:22:19,520 --> 00:22:20,717
Stubborn jackass.

334
00:22:20,800 --> 00:22:25,094
We wouldn't be able to forget about
you, even if we wanted to, Polnareff.

335
00:22:25,180 --> 00:22:26,320
You be well.

336
00:22:28,420 --> 00:22:29,460
Au River.

337
00:22:30,080 --> 00:22:30,910
Yeah.

338
00:22:31,360 --> 00:22:32,240
See you later.

339
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,150
Holly!

340
00:22:49,233 --> 00:22:51,277
How are you sitting up
straight all of a sudden?

341
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:53,220
I'm feeling much better.

342
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:55,875
I'm not sure how to put it into words.

343
00:22:55,980 --> 00:22:58,297
It's as if we could
read each other's minds.

344
00:22:58,380 --> 00:22:59,210
What?

345
00:22:59,293 --> 00:23:01,705
Mom, I can feel that
they're coming home to us.

346
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:05,220
Oh, Polly!

347
00:23:05,740 --> 00:23:07,600
Papa and my Jotaro!

348
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:10,740
They're coming home!

349
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:05,400
Thank you.

350
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:38,480
Thank you.
